<title>UK: Horlick affair not affecting business - MGAM.</title>
<headline>Horlick affair not affecting business - MGAM.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The controversy over pension fund manager Nicola Horlick is not damaging the business of Morgan Grenfell Asset Management, the firm's chief executive Robert Smith told Reuters in a telephone interview on Friday.</p>
<p>Asked whether MGAM in general or the pension fund business in particular would be hurt, Smith said, &quot;I don't think so, it's not very pretty reading, of course, and no one enjoys reading about themselves the way we're being described but I don't think it will do lasting damage.&quot;</p>
</text>
